{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/976502-advice-on-2e-court","id":976502,"title":"Advice on 2e Court","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T07:03:17-07:00","id":976502,"title":"Advice on 2e Court","content":"I'm currently planning to do a PBP of the Changeling the Lost 2e with the material currently given to us from both the playtest and other sources. For this, I've written a brief thing or the Courts of England. I'd like to get people's thoughts on the Court as I've written it so far, and suggestions perhaps on what to add. Also, for those interested in playing, <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?501715-Changeling-the-Lost-2e-The-Creature-In-The-Docklands\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showt...-The-Docklands</a> is where I'm currently recruiting. I'm unsure exactly where I will be playing the game, either these boards or Gianititp's. I will also be allowing some of the Homebrew Kiths from the thread on this forum.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">There are three Courts in the Freehold of London, the Court of the Lion, the Unicorn and the Bear.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Court of the Lion, The Woodsman, Courage</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Lions are a courageous bunch who aim to take on the challenges that are brought to them and solve them whatever the cause or cost. They are the heroes, those who stand proud and ready in the face of the Huntsmen.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They have affinities for the Contracts of Emotion (Courage) and Inspiration [This is found in the Dark Eras book and I can supply information.]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mantle - </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1 - A Lion Courtier gains an air of confidence around him, he will find the truth. Others recieve a -1 penalty when attempting to decieve you.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2 - You gain the Merit Goblin Vow (Courage).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3 - It is difficult for the Wyrd of the Hedge to stand in your way. +2 to Survival when in the Hedge, and your hair takes a golden sheen or streaks.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4 - You gain an approach relevant to the Lion Court.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5 - You radiate with a slight glow when you walk, and your inspiration can rub off on others in acts of heroism. You gain the Enchanting Performance 3 Merit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Court of the Unicorn, The Maiden, Trust</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Unicorns are those that keep the idea of trust in high regard. They trust the members of the Freehold to act on their best interests but also know who to trust with the secrets. They are the face of giving and holding back, healers and spies holding hands.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They have affinities for the Contracts of Emotion (Trust) and Vainglory.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mantle - </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1 - You hae an aura of trust around you, +1 to Empathy when Consoling others.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2 - You gain the Merit Goblin Vow (Trust).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3 - Your eyes begin to sheen with silver from time to time. You gain 9-Again on Persuasion rolls.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4 - You gain an approach relevant to the Unicorn Court.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5 - A silvery mist follows you around, you may heal another changeling once a day by touch, taking the damage dealth up to half of your health. (A Changeling with Health 10 can heal 5 damage.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Court of the Bear, The Wolf, Hunger</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Fighting is good, winning is better. The Bears have fought for what they have and they will not give it up. Whatever the want, they will strive to make it happen. Occasionally at odds with the Lions, they find Inspiring is all well and fine but sacrifice isn't the cut of their jib. They have their territories and they're going to keep them.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">They gain affinity in the Contracts of Emotion (Hunger) and Abjuration [Also in the Dark Eras books, ask if needed.]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mantle - </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1 - Gain a dot in Iron Stamina, you won't be taken down so easily. You always seem slightly bigger than you actually are.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2 - You gain the Goblin Vow merit (Hunger).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3 - You have +1 Armour permanently and the sound of your footprints when you are not hiding them seem to echo and rumble.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4 - You gain an approach relevant to the Bear Court.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5 - You gain an extra Hollow Merit 3 for Free, and a 9-Again for Weaponry when fighting in your Hollows or Territory.</span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1740-soirgriffe","name":"Soirgriffe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:50:07-07:00","id":976579,"title":"","content":"I like it well done.","signature"